# 0293 — Honest truncation: chrome labels, paths, held-back errors

Three places cut content without saying so, each in a way that removed exactly
the part worth keeping.

## Behavior changes

**`Panel` titles and footers.** Titles were contracted with `chars().take(n)`,
which counts code points rather than columns: a CJK or emoji title overran its
own border. Footers were never contracted at all. All four panel variants now
go through one grapheme-safe rule that marks the cut with the catalog ellipsis
and applies to the footer too.

```rust
// Before: a 10-character CJK title spent 20 columns and broke the frame.
Panel::new(&system).title("日本語のタイトルです、とても長い見出し")
// After: contracted to the columns the chrome can spare, border intact.
```

**Paths keep their filename.** `QuickOpen`'s detail column end-cut its paths,
so `src/widgets/quick_open.rs` became `src/widgets/quick_o…` — the one token
that tells two candidates apart. It now drops leading segments
(`…/quick_open.rs`), and when even that will not fit, the directories go
entirely and the filename alone is contracted from its middle
(`quic…en.rs`).

`text::truncate_path` changed its fallback to match: it used to middle-contract
the *whole path*, which produced `src/w…en.rs` — the directories survived and
the filename did not.

**`Form` says how many errors it is not showing.** The error summary listed
three validation errors and silently dropped the rest; five errors showed
three. It now paints a `+2 more` row below the list, and reserves the row in
its own height so the field body does not shift.

## Consumer edits

- Snapshots of a contracted panel title: the cut point moves for any title
  with non-ASCII characters, and long footers now end in `…`.
- Snapshots of a `QuickOpen` detail column: paths lead with `…/`.
- A host that read `FormState::error_summary_count` to lay out around the
  summary gets one more row when errors exceed three.

## Validation

```sh
cargo nextest run -p termrock --all-features error_summary_says
cargo nextest run -p termrock --all-features narrow_paths_keep
cargo nextest run -p termrock --all-features wide_titles_and_long
mise run check
```
